  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Sustaining the Gains: Strengthening Accountability to Gender Equality and Women&apos;s rights in Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;This is a joint programme to be implemented by four UN Agencies namely: UN Women, UNDP, UNICEF and UNFPA. The Overall Objective of the programme is to directly contribute to the implementation of the Commitment to Action and Plan of implementation of the High Level Political Compact on Ending Gender Based Violence and Harmful Practices (2021-2030). The priority focus areas for the programme are: 1) Strengthening accountability to gender equality, women&apos;s rights and women&apos;s empowerment 2). Creation of Gender and Accountability mechanisms and 3). Production of evidence-based knowledge and data on GEWE in Zimbabwe. The Specific objectives are: 1). Strengthened gender responsive governance and accountability within government institutions to ensure compliance with international, regional and national gender equality provisions 2). Improved financing for gender equality, women&apos;s rights and GBV response through national government and other relevant domestic resource mobilisation models&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
